(5582420, 807406, 54645, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>First, I enjoyed your portfolio, plenty of good work. Particularly <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=770261" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this!</a> <br/> <br/>FIRST IMPRESSION:<br/>Does not grab, as you said, bit out of the box for what I was expecting for street. <br/> <br/>COMPOSITION:<br/>Excellent. The right building is positioned well. The inclusion of the distant buildings buried in dark hurts IMO. <br/> <br/>TECHNICAL:<br/>I really like the way you capture the detailed lighting of the main building. Highlights it''s texture. Drawback...the bright lights far off on the leading lines. Visual competition!<br/> <br/>You know, when I sit here looking through the photograph, I''m drawn to the architecture of the main building, and for that reason it does not feel *street*. But you knew that based on your comments in the description. :) <br/> <br/>Cheers,<br/> <br/>Ben<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club First, I enjoyed your portfolio, plenty of good work. Particularly this!  FIRST IMPRESSION:Does not grab, as you said, bit out of the box for what I was expecting for street.  COMPOSITION:Excellent. The right building is positioned well. The inclusion of the distant buildings buried in dark hurts IMO.  TECHNICAL:I really like the way you capture the detailed lighting of the main building. Highlights it''s texture. Drawback...the bright lights far off on the leading lines. Visual competition! You know, when I sit here looking through the photograph, I''m drawn to the architecture of the main building, and for that reason it does not feel *street*. But you knew that based on your comments in the description. :)  Cheers, Ben ', '2009-07-22 01:50:35.000000', NULL, 0),
